 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No prey killed, no weapon, no blood, no slaughtered animal drawn. Light for «من يخافه بالغيب», geometric for «عزيز ذو انتقام», the sea mood and a fish only for the permitted «صيد البحر» (leaving before «وحرم عليكم صيد البر»). STAGING v4: Pilgrims in ihram (white robes) on the road with a camel (hajj shown only as travellers; no Kaaba, no sanctuary). No game, no weapon, no hunting or killing drawn. 94: they walk; on 94:15 (fearing Him unseen, holding back from the game) they bow with a lamp plate (no light plate on the pronoun of Allah) and leave with the camel on 94:16; two paths on the empty road while the transgressor's punishment is recited (94:17-23). 95: they turn away on 95:5 (do not kill game); two men enter on 95:18 and speak on 95:20 and 95:23 (two just men judge the equivalent, verse and both tafsirs) and leave; wheat for the food for the poor, hourglass for the fasting; the pilgrims bow on 95:38 (pardon of what is past) and leave on 95:41, so the threat (95:42-50) falls on the empty road with two paths, then geometric from the Name on 95:45. The camel appears only in 94 as the travellers' mount; it is not on stage in 95, so nothing reads as the livestock equivalent or the offering. 96: the pilgrims on the sea shore, fish plate for the permitted sea game (leaves before 96:9), they turn on 96:11 (land game forbidden while in ihram) and bow on 96:16 (fear Allah)."
 },
